    "irregularities": "BNBC 2020 Part 6 Sec 2.5.5.3 (pp. 617-618) with Tables 6.1.4-6.1.5 (pp. 490-491) and Figures 6.2.27-6.2.28 (pp. 619-621): re-entrant projections 15 %; openings 50 % of the gross enclosed area or a 50 % change of diaphragm stiffness; soft storey 70 % of the storey above or 80 % of the three above, extreme 60 % / 70 %; weak storey 80 % of the storey above, extreme 65 %; in-plane offset greater than the element's length; vertical geometric 130 % of an adjacent storey (Table 6.1.4 type III and Figure 6.2.28(c), L2 > 1.3 L1), a one-storey penthouse not considered. Mass: Sec 2.5.5.3.2(ii) prints twice an adjacent storey (also Figure 6.2.28(b)), Table 6.1.4 type II prints 150 percent of an adjacent storey; the more conservative 150 % is used (owner decision 2026-11-01 on apparent misprints), a roof lighter than the floor below not considered. nonparallelTolerance (5 degrees off the major axes) is SAEngine practice, not BNBC (the code gives no tolerance). strength: the storey lateral strength of the weak storey check estimated by the vertical elements' nominal shear strength, Vc = 0.17 lambda sqrt(f'c) bw d (Sec 6.4.2.1.1, Eq. 6.6.49, p. 922; walls Sec 6.4.8.5 with d = 0.8 lw, Sec 6.4.8.4, p. 936) plus the ties; d = 0.8 h of a column is SAEngine practice, not BNBC; the flexural strength of the elements can govern and is not counted (an estimate)",
