    "softStorey": "BNBC 2020 Part 6 Sec 2.5.17 (p. 666), approach (2), when Omega0 is not included: the soft storey's columns and beams for 2.5 times the storey shears and moments of the earthquake analysis (infill neglected), its symmetrically placed shear walls for 1.5 times the lateral shear; approach (1), a dynamic analysis with the infill walls and the members' inelastic deformation, is not done by SAEngine",
    "diaphragmConnections": "BNBC 2020 Part 6 Sec 1.7.3.8(d)(i) (p. 505) and Sec 2.5.5.6.2 (p. 625): Seismic Design Category D with plan irregularity type I.a, I.b, II, III or IV or vertical type IV, the Sec 2.5.7 forces of the diaphragm-to-vertical-element and collector connections +25 % (transfer.diaphragm.irregularIncrease); collectors too unless they take the Omega0 combinations. Sec 1.7.3.8(d)(ii) (p. 506): with plan type II the chords and collectors take the projecting wings moving in the same and in opposite directions, unless a dynamic analysis (Sec 2.5.8) on a three-dimensional model gives the forces",
    "timeHistory": "BNBC 2020 Part 6 Sec 2.5.10.2 (pp. 636-637): at least three ground motions; 2D: the mean of the 5 %-damped spectra of the records not less than the design spectrum (Sec 2.5.4.3) at every period from 0.2T to 1.5T; 3D: pairs with one scale factor on both components, the mean of the pairs' SRSS spectra not less than 1.3 times the design spectrum over 0.2T to 1.5T. Sec 2.5.10.3 (p. 637): orthogonal pairs applied simultaneously; where the largest base shear Vth is less than the equivalent static V (Sec 2.5.7.1), every response times V/Vth (drifts included); fewer than seven records (or pairs) the largest response, at least seven the mean; displacements and drifts times Cd/I (Sec 2.5.7.7). Sec 2.5.13.1(c) (p. 645): 3D analysis applies both directions simultaneously with ground motions of Sec 2.5.10.2 or 2.5.11.2. Sec 2.5.11.2 (pp. 639-640): the nonlinear analysis scales to the real design spectrum, Eq. 6.2.34 with R = 1 and I = 1, with the same period range and ratios (targets.nonlinear). The scaling method (each record first fitted to the spectrum over the range in log space, then one factor on the suite so that the criterion is just met) is SAEngine practice; the code asks only that the mean meets the spectrum"
